  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ad496817cc2ac7b498b32f0fc2de6fb3, type: 3}
  m_Name: R1_01_Float
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::JournalEntry
  title: Float
  pages:
  - bigIdea: Less gravity means a slower fall, so you stay in the air longer and
      go further.
    notes: 'Hold Jump while falling and the shard''s glow takes most of your weight
      away, for one second per jump. It never lifts you, it only slows the fall.
      (Real people can''t switch gravity off, of course: that part is shard magic.
      The rest is honest physics.)'
    lookCloser: "Float gravity: 29.43 \xF7 6 \u2248 4.9 m/s\xB2, so weight <color=#8a5a2e>29.4
      N</color> \u2192 <color=#8a5a2e>4.9 N</color>. Fall capped at 2 m/s, 1 s per
      jump.\nJump alone: about 4.9 m across.   With float: about 9.6 m."
    funFact: The Moon's gravity is about 1/6 of Earth's. Floating here feels like
      a Moon walk.
    marginP1: Float, then Burst from the air!
    marginP2: Hang time = aiming time.
    diagram:
      show: 1
      objectLabel: 'Player

        1 kg'
      forces:
      - label: Weight (float)
        newtons: 4.9
        direction: 3
        kind: 3
        unit: N
      caption: Normally 29.4 N. While floating, only 4.9 N.
